<section class="sec" id="faq" style="background:#fff">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow reveal">FAQ</span>
<h2 class="st reveal">The questions people actually <span class="serif">ask.</span></h2>
<p class="lede reveal">If yours isn't here, a counsellor answers it on a 20-minute call.</p>
<div class="faq-wrap">
<div class="acc reveal">
<details open=""><summary>How much math do I really need? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Enough to reason, not to prove theorems. We teach the statistics and linear algebra you need inside the modules, always tied to a model you are building. Quantitative comfort matters more than a math degree.</div></details>
<details><summary>What is the difference between this and the Data Analytics course? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Analytics answers what happened using SQL and dashboards. Data science predicts and automates decisions using models. This course includes Python at depth, ML, deep learning and GenAI, and runs six months instead of four.</div></details>
<details><summary>Will I work on GenAI or just classical ML? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both, deliberately. Classical ML remains most production work; GenAI is the fastest-growing layer. You build a RAG assistant and LLM applications alongside churn and vision models.</div></details>
<details><summary>What is the starting salary in data science? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Junior roles typically start between Rs 4 and 8 lakh depending on portfolio strength. With deployed projects and two years of experience, Rs 8 to 16 lakh is common, and GenAI skills push the top of every band.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do I need to know coding before joining? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Some exposure helps but is not required. The first month builds Python fluency from fundamentals with heavy practice. Analysts and developers can fast-track through it.</div></details>
<details><summary>Are the projects real or toy datasets? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Real and messy. Capstones use realistic business data, and every model ends behind a live endpoint recruiters can call. Toy notebooks do not survive interviews; deployed work does.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is it online or classroom, and is Malayalam support available? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both. In-person batches in Trivandrum, Kochi and Bengaluru, plus live online batches across Kerala and the GCC. Sessions are in clear English with Malayalam support.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you guarantee a job after the course? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">No, and we will not pretend otherwise. We provide structured placement support and real introductions across 400+ partners, with support continuing six months after you finish.</div></details>
</div>
<aside class="faq-aside reveal">
<div class="aside-card">
<span class="av-lg photo">[ Anjali · photo ]</span>
